cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "A transport protocol in repeating fast radio bursts, and the language-grade signal inside it"
authors:
  - family-names: Meucci
    given-names: Shiva
url: "https://github.com/steampunkphysics/frb-transport-protocol-reanalysis"
repository-code: "https://github.com/steampunkphysics/frb-transport-protocol-reanalysis"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-01"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  Complete reproducibility package for the reanalysis paper: both paper
  editions, every analysis script with committed deterministic outputs,
  figure generators, and control corpora. A reproducible reanalysis of
  "Evidence for Structured Signal Traffic in Fast Radio Burst Data"
  (doi:10.5281/zenodo.19443570): standard protocol-reverse-engineering
  criteria find a transport layer; removing it as a receiver would isolates
  a stream that passes the standard two-axis statistical language test,
  with a cross-telescope fingerprint square showing the payload statistics
  travel with the source, not the instrument.
keywords:
  - fast radio bursts
  - SETI
  - protocol reverse engineering
  - information theory
  - Shannon entropy
  - linguistic laws
  - Zipf's law
  - cross-source replication
  - reproducible research
